  "title": "Reason-IAD and CoLVR: Exploring Latent Visual Reasoning for Industrial Anomaly Detection",
  "summary": "Reason-IAD introduces a knowledge-guided dynamic latent reasoning framework for explainable industrial anomaly detection, while CoLVR enhances exploratory latent visual reasoning through contrastive optimization. Both frameworks address limitations of current methods and improve the accuracy and interpretability of anomaly detection in industrial settings.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Reason-IAD uses a retrieval-augmented knowledge module to incorporate category-specific textual descriptions into the model input, enabling context-aware reasoning over domain-specific defects.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "CoLVR employs a latent contrastive training framework to expand the semantic latent space and avoid over-constrained embedding, while also enabling fine-grained optimization of latent visual reasoning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reason-IAD achieves average improvements of 5.83% on VSP and 8.00% on Jigsaw, while CoLVR demonstrates significant improvements on out-of-domain benchmarks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
